DNS Alias populates separate PF destination tables from trusted Unbound replies.
Define exact DNS names or wildcard subdomains and select the resulting aliases
in ordinary pfSense rules. Each observed mapping retains its own remaining DNS
TTL. Clients can share a table across interfaces while each firewall rule
controls its source, ports and action.

The package includes a WebGUI for alias management, DNS observations and
firewall statistics. Plain Unbound is supported. Fresh installations start
disabled and create no traffic rules.
